# Copy this file to .env (same folder as docker-compose.yml) before starting Docker,
# fill in your mail server, REMOVE the # at the start of each setting line, then run:  docker compose up -d
# .env is ignored by Git, so the password is never committed.
# Without a .env file, every email goes to the test inbox at http://localhost:8026

# Testing only: a Gmail mailbox (needs 2-Step Verification and an App Password). Production uses Outlook below.
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_TLS=true
# SMTP_USER=your.address@gmail.com
# SMTP_PASSWORD=your-16-letter-app-password
# MAIL_FROM=your.address@gmail.com

# Your company name, shown to customers in the "thank you for your interest" email sent to new leads
# COMPANY_NAME=SRS Consulting

# Every email goes out FROM this one address (shown as "<user name> via SalesTrack");
# customer replies go to the salesperson's own email (Reply-To).

# Example: Outlook / Microsoft 365. Microsoft turned off SMTP passwords (basic auth) in 2026, so use OAuth:
# IT registers an app in Azure (Entra ID) with the Microsoft Graph "Mail.Send" application permission
# (admin consent), ideally limited to the CRM mailbox, and gives you these three values.
# MAIL_PROVIDER=graph
# MS_TENANT_ID=your-tenant-id
# MS_CLIENT_ID=your-app-client-id
# MS_CLIENT_SECRET=your-app-secret
# MAIL_FROM=crm@yourcompany.com

# Check it at http://localhost:8001/docs (log in as Admin): GET /api/health/email, then POST /api/health/email/test

# ---------- AI Assistant ----------
# The AI Assistant page is off until an OpenAI API key is set here. Restart with: docker compose up -d
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# ---------- Login ----------
# On the first start the CRM creates this Admin (only if there is no active Admin yet).
# Log in with it, change the password (profile menu > Change Password), then add users on the Users page.
# ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@salestrack.local
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=Admin@2026
# Email domains allowed for new users (comma separated). Personal emails like Gmail are refused.
# Leave it empty (ALLOWED_EMAIL_DOMAINS=) to allow any domain.
# ALLOWED_EMAIL_DOMAINS=srsconsultinginc.com
# Signs the login tokens. Put any long random text here (anyone who knows it could create logins).
# SECRET_KEY=change-this-to-a-long-random-text

# ---------- Optional: one database shared by several computers ----------
# Every login on this computer already shares one database (the "db" container).
# To have teammates' computers use the same data, point them all at one PostgreSQL server:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://crm_user:crm_pass@192.168.1.20:5433/crm_db
# APP_URL=http://192.168.1.20:5173        # link used in notification emails

# ---------- AI email drafting (optional, backend only) ----------
# Generate subject/message drafts in the email composer. Sending remains a separate action.
# Use sample for local stage-based examples without a key (not AI generation).
# EMAIL_DRAFT_MODE=sample
# Use openai for real AI drafting with the key below.
# EMAIL_DRAFT_MODE=openai
# OPENAI_API_KEY=your-openai-api-key
# OPENAI_EMAIL_MODEL=gpt-4.1-mini
# After setting the key in .env, run: docker compose up -d --build

# Docker reads OPENAI_API_KEY from this file through a read-only secret mount.
# The key is not copied to frontend code, images, or Docker environment configuration.
